  "problem": "Let $\\overset{^}{T}(t)$ be a particular solution of the differential equation from the previous part that satisfies the condition $\\overset{^}{T}(0)=28.$ Find $\\overset{^}{T}(t).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\overset{^}{T}(t)\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Previously, we found that the general solution is\n\n$$\nT=25+K{e}^{-0.03t}.\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $T(0)=28$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}28 & =25+K\\,{e}^{-0.03(0)} \\\\ 28 & =25+K\\,{e}^{0} \\\\ K & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the required particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{T}(t)=25+3{e}^{-0.03t}.\n$$",
